---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import TokenTable from "../../components/TokenTable.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Token reference"
  description="All system tokens: author form read from CSS in build, resolved value read from live browser."
>
  <h1>Token reference</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Each token in its two forms: the one that was written and the one that resolves right now, in the dimensions selected above.
  </p>

  <TokenTable />

  <h2>How to read the tiers</h2>
  <p>
    References point <strong>down or sideways, never up</strong>, and tier 3 cannot jump to tier 1. That is not convention: the validator enforces it. A <code>--ramp-*</code> within a component's CSS is the visible sign that someone skipped the semantic layer and broke dark mode for that component alone.
  </p>
  <p>
    The <span class="sk-badge" data-tone="success">component</span> tokens live on the element, not
    in <code>:root</code>, so they resolve against a test element carried by the class. Yes
    <em>appears unresolved in this context</em>, it is not a bug: it is the tier 3 scoping showing. that
    token does not exist until an element opts for it.
  </p>
</Base>
